            {
                id conformance-driver-el
                title "Differential driver for the el_* non-interactive surface, the largest untested area"
                deps (conformance-differential)
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-08-05T10:59:11.080143617Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Recommended as the next driver by the agent that built the first one, and the reasoning holds: this is the largest surface still untested, and none of it needs a tty.\n\nCover: el_init_fd against pipes; el_set and el_get across EVERY op, since the wide varargs dispatch is essentially untested — H_FUNC proved the eleven-slot path exactly once; EL_EDITOR, EL_BIND, EL_HIST; el_source against a controlled .editrc; el_parse.\n\nThat reaches map, parse, keymacro and chared, four concerns whose translate leaves are complete and whose behaviour has never been executed against the C.\n\nIt will also force the abi-file-surface decision from a second direction: EL_SETFP hits the same FILE * wall as H_SAVE_FP, so this driver will produce a second cluster of divergences with a single cause. Expect that rather than treating it as new.\n\nReuse conformance/lib.sh's pinned environment as-is. It builds the environment with env -i rather than overlaying, so an inherited EDITRC cannot leak in — which matters more for this driver than the last one, since el_source reads EDITRC and HOME directly. The four variables the C reads through el_getenv are EDITRC (src/el.c:610), HOME (:614), TERM (src/terminal.c:906) and EDITOR (src/vi.c:1112).\n\nFollow the existing conventions: trace lines are `NNNN <26-char operation label> <result>`, never a raw pointer, never a path, never strerror text — errno numeric only. Anything address-derived gets reduced to a boolean, the way H_FUNC's ref did. Run it under both LC_ALL=C.UTF-8 and LC_ALL=C; the two produce materially different results and that is real coverage rather than a repeat.\n\nAdd it to conformance/determinism.sh's list, which runs every driver three times per library per locale from a wiped directory and requires byte-identical output.\n\nAnd the standing rule from the first run: DO NOT fix the Rust to make the diff go away. Report each divergence with its governing rule and whether the register already holds it as a frozen defect."
                    }
                )
            }

